/*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*\
  elementary02 (plain-Arrhenius side) -- a CHEMKIN third-body law in a PFR, REVERSIBLE by
  detailed balance, against the Arrhenius law it equals.  nButane <=> isoButane,
  gas, isothermal 900 K, isobaric 3 bar, ideal gas, no mole change: the
  concentrations sum to P/(R T) = 40.0907850149809 mol/m3 along the whole bed.

  Both species carry third-body efficiency 2, so [M] = 2 (c_n + c_iso)
  = 80.1815700299618 mol/m3, constant.  Rate k [M] c_n (first order in nButane), and the
  reverse k [M] / Kc c_iso.  Molecularity 1 + 1 (the third body), so the
  CHEMKIN A in cm6/mol2/s is converted with (1e-6)^(2-1) in this mol/m3 reactor.
    chemkin side:  A = 3.0e8 cm6/mol2/s, b = 0.5, Ea = 25 kcal/mol (104600 J/mol)
    hand value  :  A_eq = 3.0e8 * 1e-6 * 900^0.5 * [M] = 721634.1302696562 1/s,  Ea = 104600 J/mol
  The two cases' outlets must agree to 1e-9 (bin/curate/check_elementary_rates.py).
\*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

isom
{
    reversible true;
    stoichiometry
    (
        { component nButane;    nu -1;  order 1; }
        { component isoButane;  nu  1;  order 0; }
    );
    kinetics
    {
        type   Arrhenius;
        A      721634.1302696562;
        Ea     104600.0;
    }
}
